00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:55.280
Lady, I did too.
天哪，我也写了。

144
00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:58.380
I wrote on Thursday, February 2nd, 2006,
我写道，2006年2月2日，星期四，

145
00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.800
Boys and Girls, there are many things I love about working on this show.
《男孩与女孩》，能参演这部剧有许多我喜欢的地方。

146
00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:04.540
But one of the coolest is the creative input that we get to have.
但最酷的事情之一就是我们能有创作上的投入。

147
00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:07.300
A lot of shows just don't let their actors get involved that way.
很多剧集就是不让演员以那种方式参与进来。

148
00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:12.440
But Jen and I were talking about our lives before the show, when she was a secretary and I was an operator.
但珍和我当时在聊我们拍戏前的生活，当时她是秘书，我是接线员。

149
00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:18.380
And we were laughing about all the crazy seminars and ridiculous meetings we had to sit through at our old corporate jobs.
我们在笑谈以前在公司工作时不得不坐着听的那些疯狂的研讨会和荒谬的会议。

150
00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:22.340
We sort of had this idea that it would be a funny episode called Women in the Workplace.
我们当时有了这样一个想法，觉得拍一集名叫《职场女性》的剧会很有趣。

151
00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:25.100
We ran into Greg Daniels and told him our little idea.
我们遇到了格雷格·丹尼尔斯，把我们的这个小想法告诉了他。

152
00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:27.560
We didn't have anything fleshed out or written down.
我们当时没有任何具体的细节或文字记录。

153
00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:28.940
And he got so excited.
而他兴奋极了。

154
00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:31.320
He grabbed BJ and he said, start writing this down.
他抓住BJ说，快把这个记下来。

155
00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:33.940
And BJ got a notepad and started jotting things down.
BJ于是拿出一个记事本开始记下一些东西。

156
00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:35.920
Greg started scribbling notes too.
格雷格也开始飞速记笔记。

157
00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.700
Weeks later, BJ Novak wrote this awesome script.
几周后，BJ·诺瓦克写出了这个棒极了的剧本。

158
00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:40.300
Jen and I were so excited.
珍和我当时兴奋极了。

159
00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:43.940
We are so lucky to be a part of a show that would respect our ideas.
我们太幸运了，能参演一部尊重我们想法的剧集。

160
00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:47.040
Oh, that is so nice.
哦，这太好了。

161
00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:49.400
You wrote mostly about the collaboration.
你写的内容主要关于合作。

162
00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:52.320
I wrote very differently about this in my journal.
我在日记里对此有截然不同的记录。

163
00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:54.800
Wait, can I say the last thing I wrote was,
等等，我能说我写的最后一句是，

164
00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:56.560
to any of the writers out there,
致所有的编剧们，

165
00:07:56.560 --> 00:08:00.140
we're not going to get in the habit of just bugging you guys with ideas.
我们不会养成经常用想法去烦你们的习惯。

166
00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:00.680
I know.
我知道。

167
00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:03.000
We would always have these bright ideas as a cast,
我们作为演员总会有这些绝妙的想法，

168
00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.920
and we always worried that we annoyed the writers.
而且我们总是担心会惹恼编剧。

169
00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:07.160
But they were always so receptive and nice.
但他们总是那么乐于接受并且很友善。

170
00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:07.600
I know.
我知道。

171
00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:08.480
Even if they were pretending.
哪怕他们是装出来的。

172
00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:10.180
Okay, so what did you write about?
好吧，那你写了些什么？

173
00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:17.440
Okay, I went on a very elaborate description of where we were when we came up with the idea for this episode.
好吧，我极其详尽地描述了我们想出这一集点子时的所在地。

174
00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:18.200
Where were we?
我们在哪里？

175
00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:19.220
We were in my trailer.
我们在我的房车里。

176
00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:21.840
We were having a picnic lunch.
我们在吃野餐午饭。

177
00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:22.640
Oh my gosh.
噢天哪。

178
00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:26.580
I described that we had scented candles.
我描述说我们还点着香薰蜡烛。

179
00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:32.220
I love our two different accounts of this moment in time.
我太喜欢我们俩对同一时刻的这两种不同叙述了。

180
00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:35.700
Yes, scented candles, and that we were discussing it.
对，有香薰蜡烛，而且我们正在讨论这个。

181
00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:39.000
And I also wrote that we did this all the time.
我还写到我们经常这样做。

182
00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:41.360
We would have these ladies' lunches.
我们会搞这种姐妹午餐。

183
00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:47.140
And during this ladies' lunch, we got the bright idea for this episode that we ran onto the set,
然后在这个姐妹午餐期间，我们想出了这一集的绝妙点子，我们冲到片场，

184
00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:50.480
that we set it to Greg Daniels, same as you.
把它告诉了格雷格·丹尼尔斯，和你们一样。

185
00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:54.740
He pulled BJ aside, and BJ's like, oh my gosh, what is this episode idea?
他把BJ拉到一边，BJ说，天哪，这一集的点子是什么？

186
00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:56.680
And we said, here's what it is.
然后我们说，内容是这样的。

187
00:08:56.860 --> 00:09:01.620
The idea is that Jan comes in and has a woman in the workplace seminar,
这个点子是简进来举办了一个职场女性研讨会，

188
00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:06.080
and then Michael gets jealous, and he says, I want a man in the workplace seminar.
然后迈克尔吃醋了，他说，我也要办一个职场男性研讨会。

189
00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:07.740
And BJ's like, I love it.
BJ说，我太喜欢了。

190
00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:08.640
What happens next?
接下来发生什么？

191
00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:09.540
And we're like, we don't know.
我们说，不知道。

192
00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:09.900
That's it.
就这些。

193
00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:10.660
That's all we got.
我们就这点东西。

194
00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:12.140
He's like, that's it.
他说，就这？

195
00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:12.740
That's the whole thing.
整集就这么点？

196
00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:13.320
We're like, yeah.
我们说，对啊。

197
00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:16.520
And he's like, okay, I have a lot of work to do.
然后他说，好吧，我有很多工作要做。

198
00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:18.720
And BJ filled in all the blanks.
然后BJ填补了所有的空白。

199
00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:19.300
All the reSt.
剩下的所有内容。

200
00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:27.600
Fast fact number two, another fan question from Elani Swentzel.
冷知识之二，来自埃拉尼·斯温策尔的另一个粉丝提问。

201
00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:34.080
One of my favorite things is watching you read people's Twitter or Instagram handles.
我最喜欢的事情之一就是看你读别人的推特或Instagram账号。

202
00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:39.780
Elani asked, were the scenes in the warehouse and the scenes in the conference room filmed at separate times?
埃拉尼问，仓库里的戏和会议室里的戏是分不同时间拍的吗？

203
00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:43.720
If so, where were the other cast members during that time?
如果是的话，其他演员在那期间都在哪儿？

204
00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:46.000
We got a lot of questions about this.
我们收到了很多关于这方面的提问。

205
00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:48.700
People wanted to know, did we have two different film crews?
大家想知道，我们是不是有两个不同的拍摄团队？

206
00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:49.820
How did this work?
这是怎么运作的？

207
00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:50.240
No.
没有。

208
00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:51.260
One film crew.
只有一个拍摄团队。

209
00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:56.040
There were a couple of days where all of the women came to work, and we shot our scenes.
有几天是所有女性来上班，我们拍了我们的戏。

210
00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:59.120
And then there were a couple of days where all the men came to work.
然后有几天是所有男性来上班。

211
00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:02.160
I don't know what I did, but I had the day off.
我不知道我干了什么，但我那天放假了。

212
00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:03.880
And I remember it was glorious.
我记得那可真是太爽了。

213
00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:04.740
This was rare.
这很少见。

214
00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:05.240
Yeah.
是啊。

215
00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:07.080
No, I remember being really excited.
不，我记得当时真的很兴奋。

216
00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:09.580
First of all, there was just a day where it was just all us gals.
首先，有一天只有我们这群姐妹在。

217
00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:10.740
And it was really fun.
真的非常有趣。

218
00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:12.840
I wrote about that in my diary as well.
我在日记里也写过这件事。

219
00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:22.300
And I think part of the inspiration for this episode came from our desire to do more scenes together and be with the other women in the office doing scenes.
我觉得这集的部分灵感来自于我们想拍更多对手戏，想和办公室里其他女性一起拍戏的愿望。

220
00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:29.100
And so it was a really fun week, not just because we got to hang out with the gals, but also we did have half the week off.
所以那真的是非常开心的一周，不仅是因为我们能和姐妹们聚在一起，还因为我们确实放了半周假。

221
00:10:29.180 --> 00:10:29.540
We did.
确实如此。

222
00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:30.300
Which was really cool.
这真的很酷。

223
00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:32.260
And then we had one day where we were all together.
然后有一天我们全员聚齐了。

224
00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:32.540
Yeah.
是啊。

225
00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:35.720
To film the scenes where the boys and girls are all together.
为了拍男生女生聚在一起的戏。

226
00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:36.040
I know.
我知道。

227
00:10:36.140 --> 00:10:38.300
And I remember we were kind of excited to see everybody.
我记得我们见到大家时都有点兴奋。

228
00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:38.980
We're like, hey.
我们就像是在说，嘿。

229
00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:40.140
Yeah, how's it been?
是啊，最近怎么样？

230
00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:41.360
What happened down there?
你们那边发生什么了？

231
00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:43.220
We'd been on summer vacation or something.
搞得就像我们刚度完暑假或者别的什么一样。

232
00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:44.000
Okay.
好吧。

233
00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:50.420
Fast fact number three, this episode is Jim and Pam's first fight.
速查事实之三，这一集是吉姆和帕姆的第一次吵架。

234
00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:51.980
It's a real fight.
这是一场真正的争吵。

235
00:10:52.180 --> 00:10:53.680
Yeah, this is a real fight.
是的，这是一场真正的争吵。

236
00:10:53.840 --> 00:11:01.560
Now, they got into a little bit of a, what would you call it, a disagreement in the episode, the fight, when Jim picks her up at the dojo.
现在，他们在剧里有过一点，你叫它什么来着，分歧，就是吉姆去道场接她时的那场争吵。

237
00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.360
Well, they've had a few bumpy moments.
好吧，他们之前有过一些磕磕绊绊的时刻。

238
00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:04.580
This is a fight.
这是一场吵架。

239
00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:05.600
It's not resolved.
而且没有解决。

240
00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:07.000
We'll get into it.
我们待会儿会细聊。

241
00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:07.320
Yeah.
对。

242
00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:11.600
But it's, yeah, they had some harsh words at each other.
但确实，他们互相说了些重话。

243
00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:16.860
This is also another episode where Jim and Pam are basically separated the entire episode.
这也是另一集吉姆和帕姆基本上整集都处于分开状态的剧集。

244
00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:20.680
So now we've had two episodes in a row where they're physically separated.
所以现在我们已经连续两集看到他们身体上分开了。

245
00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:25.860
In the last episode, you know, Pam and Roy were really getting along.
在上一集里，你知道的，帕姆和罗伊相处得挺好。

246
00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:30.100
And now in this episode, Jim and Pam get in a fight.
而现在这一集里，吉姆和帕姆吵了一架。

247
00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:33.340
I mean, we're building tension.
我的意思是，我们在积聚紧张感。

248
00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:34.520
We're building tension.
我们在积聚紧张感。

249
00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:36.580
We don't know what's happening with Dwight and Angela.
我们不知道德怀特和安吉拉那边怎么样了。

250
00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:40.220
They probably found a part of the day to sneak off and hook up.
他们大概找了个时间溜出去鬼混了吧。

251
00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:44.180
I think that, that's probably true.
我想那大概是真的。

252
00:11:44.740 --> 00:11:46.700
Well, those are the end of my fast facts.
好了，我的快讯到此结束。

253
00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:48.700
Why are you holding Angela Sass still?
你为什么还抓着安吉拉·萨斯不放？

254
00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:49.440
Okay, I'm waiting.
好吧，我在等着呢。

255
00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:52.180
Are we going to break or are you going to Angela Sass me first?
我们要去休息了，还是你要先对付我？

256
00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:54.240
I'm going to Angela Sass you before break.
我会在休息前对付你。

257
00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:54.600
What?
什么？

258
00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:55.480
Oh my gosh.
哦，天哪。

259
00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:55.740
All right, guys.
好了，伙计们。

260
00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:57.320
Guys, Angela Sass, coming your way.
伙计们，安吉拉·萨斯来了。

261
00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:59.560
I got a hot Angela Sass card to play.
我有一张厉害的安吉拉·萨斯牌要打。

262
00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:02.280
Right away, seven seconds.
马上，七秒钟。

263
00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:06.680
Angela is giving side eye to Jan right out of the gate.
安吉拉刚开始就对简翻了个白眼。

264
00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:07.200
It's true.
确实如此。

265
00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:10.760
There's going to be a lot of Angela snarky looks in this episode.
这一集里会有很多安吉拉冷嘲热讽的眼神。

266
00:12:11.140 --> 00:12:11.920
Seven seconds.
七秒钟。

267
00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:13.700
Look for some classic side eye.
期待一些经典的白眼吧。

268
00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:16.960
And when we, we'll go to break and then I'm going to come back.
等我们，我们先去休息，然后我会回来。

269
00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:18.440
I got some more Angela Sass.
我还有更多的安吉拉·萨斯。

270
00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:20.900
I'm glad you could get that off your cheSt.
我很高兴你能把这块心病说出来。

271
00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:21.400
What?
什么？

272
00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:22.140
Out of your hand.
从你手里。

273
00:12:22.460 --> 00:12:25.220
Seven seconds into the episode, I'm already like.
剧集刚开始七秒钟，我就已经这样了。

274
00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:26.280
You're sassing it out.
你在耍态度。

275
00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:27.380
I'm sassing it out.
我在耍态度。

276
00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:28.480
I'm throwing shade.
我在暗讽别人。

277
00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:29.740
Isn't that what the kids say?
现在年轻人不都这么说吗？

278
00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:31.320
I think throwing shade.
我觉得是暗讽。

279
00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:33.760
Do you throw shade or do you give shade?
你是“扔”暗讽还是“给”暗讽？

280
00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:35.300
I think you throw it.
我觉得是“扔”。

281
00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:36.120
We throw.
我们扔。

282
00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:37.460
Do you chunk shade?
你会抛暗讽吗？

283
00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:40.100
I think you chuck shade.
我觉得是抛暗讽。

284
00:12:40.220 --> 00:12:41.380
You chunk shade.
你抛暗讽。

285
00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:42.700
All right, let's go to break.
好了，我们去休息吧。

286
00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:53.660
The cold open of boys and girls.
《男女之间》的冷开场。

287
00:12:53.820 --> 00:12:54.680
Let's jump in.
我们开始吧。

288
00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:55.060
Okay.
好的。

289
00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:57.280
We open on the conference room.
我们在会议室开场。

290
00:12:57.520 --> 00:12:59.560
The women in the office are seated with Jan.
办公室的女性们和简坐在一起。

291
00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:01.320
Side eye.
白眼。

292
00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:02.820
Side eye from Angela.
安吉拉翻了个白眼。

293
00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:03.330
Side eye.
白眼。

294
00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:07.900
Pam has a talking head where she explains it's women in the workplace seminar day and that
帕姆有一个单人访谈镜头，她解释说今天是职场女性研讨会日，而且

295
00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:12.240
Michael is not invited because Jan said that five times.
迈克尔没有被邀请，因为简说了五遍。

296
00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:12.940
Five times.
整整五遍。

297
00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:13.640
He's not invited.
他没有被邀请。

298
00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:18.240
But Michael comes in anyway and interrupts the meeting.
但迈克尔还是进来了，打断了会议。

299
00:13:19.100 --> 00:13:21.160
Angela, you are wearing light pink.
安吉拉，你穿着浅粉色。

300
00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:22.740
I'm wearing light pink.
我穿着浅粉色。

301
00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:24.380
Is this because you're in love with Dwight?
这是因为你爱上德怀特了吗？

302
