00:45:20.210 --> 00:45:21.710
Are you planning to have everybody on?
你们打算让所有人都上节目吗？

1100
00:45:21.930 --> 00:45:22.330
Yes.
是的。

1101
00:45:22.490 --> 00:45:23.470
Yes, we would love that.
是的，我们很乐意。

1102
00:45:23.590 --> 00:45:23.990
Everyone.
所有人。

1103
00:45:24.210 --> 00:45:24.450
Yes.
对。

1104
00:45:24.590 --> 00:45:25.350
We're reaching out.
我们在联系。

1105
00:45:25.490 --> 00:45:26.350
Multiple times.
好多次。

1106
00:45:26.370 --> 00:45:27.010
Don't worry.
别担心。

1107
00:45:27.010 --> 00:45:32.190
We have a few episodes ahead of us, so hopefully we'll get a lot of people on.
我们后面还有好几集，所以希望我们能请到很多人来。

1108
00:45:32.370 --> 00:45:39.830
At 13 minutes, 23 seconds during this whole scene about unions, Creed is reading a newspaper.
在整场关于工会的戏进行到13分23秒时，克里德正在看一份报纸。

1109
00:45:40.610 --> 00:45:42.790
You guys, it's the Scranton Times.
伙计们，那是《斯克兰顿时报》。

1110
00:45:43.270 --> 00:45:43.830
Nice.
不错。

1111
00:45:44.090 --> 00:45:47.350
Because Phil would get the Scranton Times delivered to us.
因为菲尔会给我们订《斯克兰顿时报》。

1112
00:45:47.530 --> 00:45:47.790
Phil Shea.
菲尔·谢伊。

1113
00:45:47.930 --> 00:45:49.850
Phil Shea, prop master.
菲尔·谢伊，道具师。

1114
00:45:50.730 --> 00:45:54.950
And so whenever there was a newspaper anywhere, it was the Scranton Times.
所以无论哪里出现报纸，那都是《斯克兰顿时报》。

1115
00:45:54.970 --> 00:45:58.190
And I loved that detail then, and I love it now.
我当时就喜欢这个细节，现在依然喜欢。

1116
00:45:58.370 --> 00:45:58.970
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

1117
00:45:59.070 --> 00:46:03.810
I remember reading one one time in the back of a scene, and there had been a really big
我记得有一次在一场戏的背景里看了一期，当时有一场非常大的

1118
00:46:03.810 --> 00:46:04.850
snow storm.
暴风雪。

1119
00:46:05.050 --> 00:46:07.830
And I was reading about the snow in Pennsylvania.
我当时在读关于宾夕法尼亚州降雪的报道。

1120
00:46:08.050 --> 00:46:08.310
Yeah.
是啊。

1121
00:46:08.910 --> 00:46:09.430
All right.
好吧。

1122
00:46:09.550 --> 00:46:11.690
Well, things are about to really heat up.
好了，接下来事情真的要白热化了。

1123
00:46:11.790 --> 00:46:13.590
There's going to be some tension.
会有些紧张气氛。

1124
00:46:13.970 --> 00:46:14.150
Yeah.
对。

1125
00:46:14.270 --> 00:46:14.930
Should we take a break?
我们要休息一下吗？

1126
00:46:15.030 --> 00:46:16.750
Let's take a break, and then we're going to get into it.
我们休息一下，然后就开始进入正题。

1127
00:46:16.870 --> 00:46:17.150
All right.
好的。

1128
00:46:26.770 --> 00:46:33.510
We are back, but I'm the only one talking, because Angela is being silent.
我们回来了，但只有我在说话，因为安吉拉在沉默。

1129
00:46:33.870 --> 00:46:36.270
Angela, I need to talk about your hair today.
安吉拉，我今天得聊聊你的头发。

1130
00:46:36.270 --> 00:46:37.030
I'm sorry.
对不起。

1131
00:46:37.310 --> 00:46:41.030
It is a hot mess.
简直是一团糟。

1132
00:46:41.110 --> 00:46:42.410
What happened to you?
你经历了什么？

1133
00:46:42.530 --> 00:46:45.950
I showered this morning before I took Isabel to school.
我今天早上送伊莎贝尔去学校前洗了头。

1134
00:46:46.130 --> 00:46:46.270
Yeah.
嗯。

1135
00:46:46.370 --> 00:46:48.530
And my goal was to show up here clean.
我的目标就是干干净净地出现在这里。

1136
00:46:48.970 --> 00:46:49.770
You are clean.
你是挺干净的。

1137
00:46:49.790 --> 00:46:50.870
That's as far as I got.
我就进行到这一步。

1138
00:46:51.070 --> 00:46:52.790
So I got Isabel to school on time.
所以我按时把伊莎贝尔送到了学校。

1139
00:46:52.790 --> 00:46:54.170
I was really happy about that.
我对此真的很高兴。

1140
00:46:54.170 --> 00:46:58.330
And I drove here with wet hair, and I was like, oh, I'll freeze.
我湿着头发开车来这里，当时我想，哦，我会冻僵的。

1141
00:46:58.330 --> 00:46:59.690
I will freeze there.
我到那儿会冻僵的。

1142
00:46:59.830 --> 00:47:00.590
It's so cold.
太冷了。

1143
00:47:00.610 --> 00:47:04.430
So I kind of put my window down, and I let the wind kind of dry my hair.
所以我把车窗摇下来一点，让风把我的头发吹干。

1144
00:47:04.430 --> 00:47:05.630
This is explaining it all.
这就全说得通了。

1145
00:47:05.930 --> 00:47:10.910
And now I have this wind-dried hair from the freeway.
现在我顶着这头从高速公路上风干的头发。

1146
00:47:11.850 --> 00:47:12.290
Yeah.
是啊。

1147
00:47:12.510 --> 00:47:12.970
You do.
确实如此。

1148
00:47:13.150 --> 00:47:13.530
I do.
我是。

1149
00:47:13.650 --> 00:47:14.610
I do, guys.
我是，伙计们。

1150
00:47:14.790 --> 00:47:16.490
And you know what?
你知道吗？

1151
00:47:16.490 --> 00:47:18.310
I feel fantastic.
我感觉棒极了。

1152
00:47:19.610 --> 00:47:21.970
I, you know, I love it.
我，你知道的，我很喜欢。

1153
00:47:22.210 --> 00:47:23.130
You know I love it.
你知道我很喜欢。

1154
00:47:23.130 --> 00:47:25.510
I look like Medusa a little bit.
我看起来有点像美杜莎。

1155
00:47:26.010 --> 00:47:26.670
You know.
你懂的。

1156
00:47:26.850 --> 00:47:29.730
But it's dry, and I'm not cold, and I'm clean.
但它是干的，而且我不冷，我也很干净。

1157
00:47:30.090 --> 00:47:32.090
And I got Isabel to school on time.
我准时把伊莎贝尔送到了学校。

1158
00:47:32.310 --> 00:47:32.550
Goals.
目标达成。

1159
00:47:33.070 --> 00:47:33.390
Okay.
好的。

1160
00:47:33.890 --> 00:47:39.530
When we come back, Michael busts into the women's meeting to tell Jan that the warehouse
当我们回来时，迈克尔闯进女性会议，告诉简仓库

1161
00:47:39.530 --> 00:47:40.830
wants to start a union.
想要成立工会。

1162
00:47:41.270 --> 00:47:45.250
And Jan is like, Michael, no, there cannot be a union.
而简的反应是，迈克尔，不，绝对不能有工会。

1163
00:47:45.370 --> 00:47:46.930
You didn't agree to this, right, Michael?
你没有答应这个吧，对吧，迈克尔？

1164
00:47:47.070 --> 00:47:51.170
Like, the men in the warehouse weren't chanting, Michael, Michael, just two minutes ago, right?
就像，仓库里的男人们几分钟前才不是在喊着迈克尔、迈克尔，对吧？

1165
00:47:51.270 --> 00:47:53.010
And he's like, no, I definitely.
然后他说，不，我绝对……

1166
00:47:53.630 --> 00:47:56.450
He says something that would have made me go nuts.
他说了一句会让我抓狂的话。

1167
00:47:56.610 --> 00:47:58.950
He says, okay, don't be hysterical.
他说，好吧，别歇斯底里了。

1168
00:47:59.110 --> 00:47:59.490
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1169
00:47:59.490 --> 00:48:01.790
Oh, that's like you need to calm down.
哦，这就好像你在说需要冷静点。

1170
00:48:01.950 --> 00:48:03.570
That's like one of those kind of phrases.
这就属于那种类型的话。

1171
00:48:03.830 --> 00:48:04.430
Yeah, that's a trigger.
对，那是个雷区。

1172
00:48:04.650 --> 00:48:04.970
Oh.
哦。

1173
00:48:05.290 --> 00:48:06.390
That's a trigger for sure.
那绝对是个雷区。

1174
00:48:06.610 --> 00:48:09.310
And Pam, you're like, your reaction is hilarious.
还有帕姆，你的反应太搞笑了。

1175
00:48:09.570 --> 00:48:11.730
Once again, you have all of these facial reactions.
又一次，你做出了所有这些面部表情。

1176
00:48:12.230 --> 00:48:14.610
I had so much fun during this episode.
我在这一集里玩得太开心了。

1177
00:48:14.910 --> 00:48:18.950
Well, when we go down to the warehouse again, I loved this moment.
嗯，当我们再次下到仓库时，我超爱这个时刻。

1178
00:48:19.310 --> 00:48:24.810
The scene when the sales guys are unpacking the truck, and Ryan says,
就是销售人员在卸货的那场戏，瑞恩说，

1179
00:48:25.030 --> 00:48:28.410
you guys, we could get this job quicker if we form an assembly line.
伙计们，如果我们组装一条流水线，这活儿能干得更快。

1180
00:48:28.410 --> 00:48:32.750
And Stanley cuts him off and says, this is a run out the clock situation.
而斯坦利打断他说，这是一场混日子耗时间的局。

1181
00:48:32.750 --> 00:48:33.050
Yeah.
对。

1182
00:48:33.570 --> 00:48:34.510
Just like upstairs.
就像楼上一样。

1183
00:48:34.810 --> 00:48:36.150
I'm going to break it down to you, kid.
我来跟你讲清楚，孩子。

1184
00:48:36.390 --> 00:48:37.550
This is how we're doing this.
我们是这么干的。

1185
00:48:37.770 --> 00:48:41.550
We are not going to hypothesize on how to be more efficient.
我们不会去假设怎样才能更有效率。

1186
00:48:41.690 --> 00:48:43.770
This is just what gets done gets done.
这就是能干多少就干多少。

1187
00:48:43.890 --> 00:48:44.730
Run out the clock.
混日子。

1188
00:48:44.830 --> 00:48:46.130
Run out the clock situation.
混日子耗时间的局。

1189
00:48:46.530 --> 00:48:49.530
I was watching this with my daughter, and she goes, mom, what does he mean?
我和女儿一起看的时候，她问，妈妈，他是什么意思？

1190
00:48:49.870 --> 00:48:52.550
And I said, Isabel, he wants to do the bare minimum.
我说，伊莎贝尔，他是想敷衍了事。

1191
00:48:52.950 --> 00:48:53.230
Yeah.
对。

1192
00:48:53.350 --> 00:48:53.850
The bare minimum.
只做最少的事。

1193
00:48:54.070 --> 00:48:55.890
She was like, I kind of get that.
她说，我有点懂了。

1194
00:48:56.490 --> 00:48:57.370
But I get it.
但我懂的。

1195
00:48:58.030 --> 00:49:00.270
I've been in a lot of run out the clock situations.
我经历过很多混日子的局。

1196
00:49:01.070 --> 00:49:06.090
So when we go back upstairs, Jan starts explaining sports terMs.
所以当我们回到楼上，简开始解释体育术语。

1197
00:49:06.350 --> 00:49:07.270
Sports metaphors.
体育隐喻。

1198
00:49:07.470 --> 00:49:07.950
To the women.
向女员工们解释。

1199
00:49:08.150 --> 00:49:09.750
It's how women might be left out in the workplace.
这就是女性在职场中如何被边缘化的。

1200
00:49:09.810 --> 00:49:11.710
I'm like, is this the 1950s?
我想，这是1950年代吗？

1201
00:49:11.750 --> 00:49:12.170
I know.
我懂。

1202
00:49:12.390 --> 00:49:13.590
This was so dated.
这太老气了。

1203
00:49:13.610 --> 00:49:19.310
This felt like a little bit like it was out of like some manual, like from 1953 or something.
这感觉有点像照本宣科，就像1953年的手册一样。

1204
00:49:19.310 --> 00:49:24.170
Well, at this point, Kelly pretends like she doesn't know what second base means.
好吧，在这个时候，凯莉假装不知道二垒是什么意思。

1205
00:49:24.490 --> 00:49:27.750
She says, okay, well, Michael said he got to second base with you.
她说，好吧，迈克尔说他跟你到二垒了。

1206
00:49:27.870 --> 00:49:29.370
Does that mean you closed a sale?
这意思是说你谈成了一笔生意吗？

1207
00:49:29.890 --> 00:49:30.550
Guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1208
00:49:30.550 --> 00:49:31.610
Is that what second base means?
二垒是那个意思吗？

1209
00:49:31.830 --> 00:49:32.530
Guess what happened?
你猜发生了什么？

1210
00:49:32.530 --> 00:49:34.710
And this is a real rare thing.
这可真是极其罕见的事。

1211
00:49:34.850 --> 00:49:37.410
This is like seeing an albino rhino in the wild.
这就好比在野外看到一头白化犀牛。

1212
00:49:37.590 --> 00:49:37.830
What?
什么？

1213
00:49:38.250 --> 00:49:39.410
Angela laughs.
安吉拉笑了。

1214
00:49:39.650 --> 00:49:40.110
Yes.
是的。

1215
00:49:41.070 --> 00:49:43.150
15 minutes, 10 seconds.
15分10秒。

1216
00:49:44.550 --> 00:49:46.550
Fan question from Jeff Ackerman.
来自杰夫·阿克曼的粉丝提问。

1217
00:49:46.750 --> 00:49:47.490
He pointed it out.
他指出了这一点。

1218
00:49:47.670 --> 00:49:53.410
There is a cutaway shot of Pam and Angela after Kelly plays dumb and asks Jan what second base means.
在凯莉装傻问简二垒是什么意思之后，有一个帕姆和安吉拉的切出镜头。

1219
00:49:53.650 --> 00:49:57.530
Was that scripted or was it so funny you couldn't keep a straight face?
那是剧本写的，还是因为太好笑而憋不住笑场了？

1220
00:49:57.690 --> 00:49:59.890
That is me and Angela laughing.
那是我和安吉拉在笑。

1221
00:50:00.130 --> 00:50:00.890
We're laughing.
我们在笑。

1222
00:50:01.090 --> 00:50:01.490
We're laughing.
我们在笑。

1223
00:50:01.610 --> 00:50:10.150
But I also knew that my character really thought that Jan was just like, well, she says she looks whorish.
但我也知道，我的角色其实觉得简就是……嗯，她说简看起来像个荡妇。

1224
00:50:10.150 --> 00:50:15.330
So, she clearly doesn't think highly of Jan and judges her.
所以，她显然对简没有好感并且在评判她。

1225
00:50:15.450 --> 00:50:20.710
And so, for Kelly to call her out, Angela thoroughly enjoyed that moment.
因此，对于凯莉当面拆穿简，安吉拉非常享受那一刻。

1226
00:50:20.950 --> 00:50:22.850
I have an observation about this episode.
我对这集有一个观察。

1227
00:50:22.930 --> 00:50:23.370
Oh, yes.
哦，是的。

1228
00:50:23.370 --> 00:50:26.770
And I'm going to get right up on my soapbox and shout it.
我要立刻站上我的肥皂箱大声说出来。

1229
00:50:26.810 --> 00:50:26.990
Here we go.
我们开始吧。

1230
00:50:27.170 --> 00:50:28.010
Here we go.
我们开始吧。

1231
00:50:28.230 --> 00:50:36.510
While re-watching this episode, I noticed that the people who are hardest on Jan and her ambition are other women.
在重看这集时，我注意到对简及其野心最苛刻的其实是其他女性。

1232
00:50:36.650 --> 00:50:36.870
Yeah.
是啊。

1233
00:50:37.370 --> 00:50:37.950
Other women.
其他女性。

1234
00:50:37.950 --> 00:50:40.570
Angela calls her a slut for the way she dresses.
安吉拉因为她的穿着骂她是荡妇。

1235
00:50:40.890 --> 00:50:43.590
Pam is constantly rolling her eyes at her.
帕姆一直在对她翻白眼。

1236
00:50:43.750 --> 00:50:48.770
And then Kelly shames her slash embarrasses her for making out with Michael.
然后凯莉因为她和迈克尔亲热而羞辱她、令她难堪。

1237
00:50:49.050 --> 00:50:52.550
Then they lay into her for not being a mother.
接着她们又因为她不是个母亲而对她大加挞伐。

1238
00:50:53.050 --> 00:50:53.390
Yeah.
是啊。

1239
00:50:53.850 --> 00:50:59.310
Oftentimes, it is other women who make ambition hardest for women.
通常情况下，让女性在追求野心时感到最艰难的往往是其他女性。

1240
00:50:59.310 --> 00:51:06.630
I wondered if BJ intended to point this out or if it was a happy accident because, you know what?
我在想BJ是有意指出这一点，还是这纯属巧合，因为你懂的？

1241
00:51:06.870 --> 00:51:09.190
Jan is so excited to help Pam.
简是那么热心地想要帮助帕姆。

1242
00:51:09.530 --> 00:51:12.850
She wants to help these other women rise up.
她想帮助这些其他的女性崛起。

1243
00:51:13.030 --> 00:51:13.270
Right.
对的。

1244
00:51:13.270 --> 00:51:14.090
She is so excited.
她是那么兴奋。

1245
00:51:14.450 --> 00:51:14.890
Now, listen.
现在，听我说。

1246
00:51:14.890 --> 00:51:21.070
I think that it is totally valid when Phyllis says, I'm happy with my choices.
我觉得菲利斯说“我对自己的选择很满意”，这完全合情合理。

1247
00:51:21.390 --> 00:51:21.550
Yeah.
是啊。

1248
00:51:21.610 --> 00:51:22.730
We don't all need to be you.
我们不需要人人都成为你。

1249
00:51:22.970 --> 00:51:27.470
Not all women or all people need to be ambitious or share ambitions.
并非所有的女性或所有人都需要有野心或怀揣相同的野心。

1250
00:51:28.450 --> 00:51:34.290
But they are really hard on her and unaccepting of her for wanting to be her.
但她们对她真的太苛刻了，而且无法接受她想要做她自己。

1251
00:51:35.010 --> 00:51:37.650
Like, Phyllis is like, I'm going to be me.
就好像，菲利斯就是，我做我自己。

1252
00:51:38.130 --> 00:51:40.290
But then they're kind of hard on Jan for being Jan.
但他们对简做自己却有点严苛。

1253
00:51:40.290 --> 00:51:44.410
Well, I think Phyllis is probably the most fair of everyone.
嗯，我觉得菲利斯可能是所有人中最公正的。

1254
00:51:44.670 --> 00:51:44.970
True.
确实。

1255
00:51:45.210 --> 00:51:52.490
She's really happy with her life choices and stands by them and is unapologetic and has a very happy life.
她对自己的生活选择真的很满意，坚定不移，毫无歉意，生活非常幸福。

1256
00:51:52.670 --> 00:51:58.470
And I don't think that she wishes for Jan not to have anything.
而且我不觉得她希望简一无所有。

1257
00:51:58.690 --> 00:52:01.090
I think Phyllis is happy that Jan has chosen her path.
我觉得菲利斯为简选择了自己的道路感到高兴。

1258
00:52:01.090 --> 00:52:05.010
But everyone else in the room is snarky towards Jan.
但房间里的其他人对简冷嘲热讽。

1259
00:52:05.150 --> 00:52:05.310
Yeah.
对啊。

1260
00:52:05.430 --> 00:52:05.790
They are.
确实如此。

1261
00:52:05.790 --> 00:52:12.930
And I think one of the things I love about our friendship, and you and I both have, like,
而且我觉得我最喜欢我们的友谊的一点，你我都有，比如，

1262
00:52:12.930 --> 00:52:19.910
a group of female friends who are really about supporting one another and building each other up and encouraging each other.
有一群女性朋友，她们真的是在互相支持、互相成就、互相鼓励。

1263
00:52:20.010 --> 00:52:23.070
And you really need those women in your life.
你生命中真的很需要这样的女性。

1264
00:52:23.170 --> 00:52:23.330
Yeah.
是的。

1265
00:52:23.830 --> 00:52:24.670
You really do.
真的非常需要。

1266
00:52:24.910 --> 00:52:25.270
Yeah.
对。

1267
00:52:25.790 --> 00:52:32.790
Because that really, the momentum that women give one another is really the momentum that moves us forward.
因为真的，女性之间给予彼此的动力，才是真正推动我们前进的动力。

1268
00:52:32.930 --> 00:52:33.390
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1269
00:52:33.850 --> 00:52:34.370
Mostly.
大体上是这样。

1270
00:52:34.370 --> 00:52:36.230
All right, Jenna, step on down.
好吧，珍娜，请发表高见吧。

1271
00:52:36.510 --> 00:52:37.010
I'm stepping down.
我在发表高见呢。

1272
00:52:37.030 --> 00:52:37.590
Step down.
请讲。

1273
00:52:37.710 --> 00:52:38.250
I like it.
我很喜欢。

1274
00:52:38.290 --> 00:52:39.210
I like what you had to say.
我喜欢你刚刚说的话。

1275
00:52:39.510 --> 00:52:39.850
All right.
好的。

1276
00:52:39.950 --> 00:52:40.970
I'm off my soapbox.
我的高谈阔论就到这里。

1277
00:52:41.010 --> 00:52:48.090
Well, here's a juxtaposition to your soapbox moment, which I thought was really just well said.
好吧，与你刚才那番高谈阔论形成对比的是，我觉得那番话真的说得很好。

1278
00:52:48.330 --> 00:52:48.670
Thanks.
谢谢。

1279
00:52:48.910 --> 00:52:51.490
Here's at 15 minutes, 59 seconds.
这里是15分59秒。

1280
00:52:51.650 --> 00:52:51.830
Yep.
没错。

1281
00:52:52.070 --> 00:52:54.370
Michael puts packing peanuts into a fan.
迈克尔把包装用的塑料泡沫倒进风扇里。

1282
00:52:54.590 --> 00:52:55.290
What a dick.
真是个混蛋。

1283
00:52:56.150 --> 00:52:57.330
That's what I had to say.
这就是我要说的。

1284
00:52:57.530 --> 00:52:58.630
That's my deep thought.
这就是我的深刻思考。

1285
00:52:58.910 --> 00:52:59.390
Oh.
哦。

1286
00:52:59.390 --> 00:53:04.210
Well, Jan gets so annoyed that she goes down to the warehouse.
好吧，简气得直奔仓库。

1287
00:53:04.530 --> 00:53:04.710
Yeah.
对。

1288
00:53:04.990 --> 00:53:10.970
And this is when Jan tells the warehouse that if they unionize, they're all going to lose their jobs.
这就是简告诉仓库工人，如果他们成立工会，所有人都会失业的时候。

1289
00:53:11.150 --> 00:53:11.290
Right.
没错。

1290
00:53:11.490 --> 00:53:13.770
Very, very, very anti-union.
非常、非常、非常反工会。

1291
00:53:13.770 --> 00:53:14.470
Yes.
是的。

1292
00:53:14.650 --> 00:53:16.050
And I read, actually,
其实我还读到过，

1293
00:53:16.190 --> 00:53:32.590
that this episode has been used in law classes that deal with companies who have unions and who want to form unions and that it has been used to show the pressure and the hard road that they can have in those moments.
这一集曾被用在处理有工会以及想要组建工会的公司的法学课上，被用来展示他们在那些时刻所面临的压力和艰难险阻。

1294
00:53:32.590 --> 00:53:37.470
All right, guys, we're going to get into some sad times now for Jim and Pam.
好了，各位，接下来我们要聊聊吉姆和帕姆的一些悲伤时刻了。

1295
00:53:38.030 --> 00:53:38.250
Ooh.
噢。

1296
00:53:38.670 --> 00:53:39.250
Oh, boy.
天哪。

1297
00:53:39.510 --> 00:53:39.650
Yeah.
是啊。

1298
00:53:40.090 --> 00:53:41.750
Jim comes upstairs to make a phone call.
吉姆上楼去打电话。

1299
00:53:42.030 --> 00:53:49.970
Pam excuses herself from her meeting, and she very excitedly tells Jim about this internship opportunity in graphic design.
帕姆从会议中抽身出来，兴奋地向吉姆讲述这个平面设计的实习机会。

1300
00:53:50.690 --> 00:53:53.350
Jim adorably encourages her immediately.
吉姆非常可爱地立刻鼓励了她。

1301
00:53:53.550 --> 00:53:55.590
He's like, well, what are the details?
他就说，好吧，细节是什么？

1302
00:53:55.650 --> 00:53:56.450
I think you should do it.
我觉得你应该去做。

1303
00:53:56.730 --> 00:53:57.190
I know.
我知道。

1304
00:53:57.570 --> 00:53:59.050
And she just lights up.
然后她的眼睛一下子就亮了。

1305
00:53:59.050 --> 00:54:04.690
She needed someone to give her permission in a way to go for this.
在某种程度上，她需要有人给她允许去追求这个。

1306
00:54:04.950 --> 00:54:06.670
And Jim immediately did.
而吉姆立刻就这么做了。

1307
00:54:06.790 --> 00:54:07.110
Yes.
是的。

1308
00:54:07.110 --> 00:54:07.830
Because he's her soulmate.
因为他是她的灵魂伴侣。

1309
00:54:08.090 --> 00:54:08.430
Yes.
是的。

1310
00:54:10.030 --> 00:54:12.970
So you kind of get the sense she's going to go for it.
所以你大概能感觉到她要放手去做了。

1311
00:54:13.010 --> 00:54:14.510
But then you see a scene.
但接着你看到了一个镜头。

1312
00:54:14.650 --> 00:54:15.710
It's a spy shot.
这是一张偷拍照。

1313
00:54:15.870 --> 00:54:16.630
There's no dialogue.
里面没有对话。

1314
00:54:16.910 --> 00:54:18.150
She's holding the pamphlet.
她拿着小册子。

1315
00:54:18.590 --> 00:54:20.470
She's telling Roy about the program.
她正在向罗伊讲述这个项目。

1316
00:54:20.510 --> 00:54:24.090
And it's very clear that he is not supportive.
很明显他并不支持。

1317
00:54:24.290 --> 00:54:25.690
He sees it as a waste of time.
他觉得这是在浪费时间。

1318
00:54:25.690 --> 00:54:30.450
So we cut to this Pam talking head, and she starts talking about this house with a terrace.
所以镜头切到了帕姆的单人采访，她开始谈论一栋带露台的房子。

1319
00:54:30.950 --> 00:54:32.670
Oh, this house with a terrace.
哦，这栋带露台的房子。

1320
00:54:32.870 --> 00:54:36.070
This metaphor broke my heart.
这个比喻让我心碎。

1321
00:54:36.370 --> 00:54:36.830
Yeah.
是啊。

1322
00:54:37.050 --> 00:54:42.910
She says she was a little girl, and she read this book, and there was a house with a terrace with flowers.
她说她小时候读过一本书，里面有一栋带露台和鲜花的房子。

1323
00:54:43.530 --> 00:54:48.010
And she describes it in detail, and she says, I just always wanted that.
她详细描述了它，然后说，我一直就想要这个。

1324
00:54:48.130 --> 00:54:51.030
But, you know, it's just, you know.
但是，你知道，这只是，你知道的。

1325
00:54:51.330 --> 00:54:53.470
They don't even have those kind of houses in Scranton.
斯克兰顿根本没有那种房子。

1326
00:54:53.470 --> 00:54:54.250
They don't even have those in Scranton.
斯克兰顿连那种房子都没有。

1327
00:54:54.950 --> 00:54:57.930
Well, this was based on a story of mine.
好吧，这其实是根据我的一个故事改编的。

1328
00:54:59.230 --> 00:55:00.890
BJ came up to me on the set.
BJ 在片场找到了我。

1329
00:55:00.890 --> 00:55:02.310
We were working on a different episode.
我们当时在拍另一集。

1330
00:55:02.310 --> 00:55:03.670
He was writing this episode.
他在写这一集。

1331
00:55:03.730 --> 00:55:08.590
And he came up to me, and he said, Jenna, I've got this moment I'm trying to write.
他走到我面前说，珍娜，我这儿有个情节正在构思。

1332
00:55:09.050 --> 00:55:19.170
Was there ever a dream that you had as a little girl that has gone unrealized because it seemed unrealistic to you?
你小时候有没有过什么梦想，因为觉得不切实际而最终破灭了？

1333
00:55:19.390 --> 00:55:21.310
He said it can be really simple, though.
不过他说可以很简单。

1334
00:55:21.470 --> 00:55:22.830
It's a little girl's dream.
这是一个小女孩的梦想。

1335
00:55:23.730 --> 00:55:25.390
And I said, yes.
我说，有啊。

1336
00:55:25.650 --> 00:55:27.090
How smart is that, though?
不过这问题多聪明啊？

1337
00:55:27.230 --> 00:55:27.550
I know.
我知道。

1338
00:55:27.730 --> 00:55:28.810
BJ is so smart.
BJ 太聪明了。

1339
00:55:28.810 --> 00:55:30.230
Isn't that such a great question?
这不是一个超级棒的问题吗？

1340
00:55:30.230 --> 00:55:31.270
It's so wonderful.
太美妙了。

1341
00:55:31.530 --> 00:55:35.550
Writers, most of their job is just asking the right questions.
编剧们，他们的大部分工作就是问对问题。

1342
00:55:35.870 --> 00:55:37.190
BJ is so smart.
BJ 太聪明了。

1343
00:55:37.190 --> 00:55:39.150
Okay, so what your answer was?
好啦，那你当时的回答是什么？

1344
00:55:39.250 --> 00:55:40.450
My answer was, yes.
我的回答是，有。

1345
00:55:40.670 --> 00:55:43.150
When I was younger, I read this book.
我小的时候，读过这样一本书。

1346
00:55:43.410 --> 00:55:47.810
And in the book, there was a girl who moved into a new house with her family.
书里有个女孩和家人搬进了一栋新房子。

1347
00:55:47.950 --> 00:55:53.030
And the house had a tower, sort of like a castle might.
这房子有个塔楼，有点像城堡那样。

1348
00:55:53.030 --> 00:55:59.970
It was this tower room on the side of the house, and there was one set of stairs that went up to it.
房子侧面有一个塔楼房间，只有一套楼梯能上去。

1349
00:56:00.050 --> 00:56:05.210
And so there was this one circular room on the third floor of their home.
所以他们家的三楼有一个圆形房间。

1350
00:56:05.210 --> 00:56:11.130
And this was her space that she declared was hers to sit and think and create.
这就是她宣称属于她自己的空间，用来坐着、思考和创作。

1351
00:56:12.230 --> 00:56:16.950
And I had such a clear vision of what this tower room was.
而且我对这个塔楼房间是什么样有着非常清晰的想象。

1352
00:56:17.090 --> 00:56:24.350
And I remember thinking to myself, one day, I'm going to have a house with a circular tower room where I will create.
我还记得当时心想，总有一天，我要买下一栋带圆形塔楼房间的房子，并在那里进行创作。

1353
00:56:25.470 --> 00:56:29.810
And I've never had it, and I never got it, because who builds houses like that?
但我从来没有过，也从来没实现过，因为谁会建那种房子呢？

1354
00:56:29.970 --> 00:56:32.330
I think this dream, do not let it go.
我觉得这个梦想，千万别放弃。

1355
00:56:32.530 --> 00:56:33.090
I think-
我觉得——

1356
00:56:33.090 --> 00:56:33.830
Maybe one day.
也许总有一天吧。

1357
00:56:33.850 --> 00:56:39.170
One day, maybe, you know, they'll be like, you know, Jenna Fisher, she lives in a tower.
也许总有一天，你知道的，他们会说，你看，詹娜·费舍，她住在一座塔里。

1358
00:56:40.230 --> 00:56:45.910
She has a very normal-looking house, and then next to it, she has built this tower.
她有一栋看起来很正常的房子，然后在旁边，她建了这座塔。

1359
00:56:46.690 --> 00:56:47.170
In Missouri.
在密苏里州。

1360
00:56:47.850 --> 00:56:48.870
It's very strange.
这太奇怪了。

1361
00:56:49.530 --> 00:56:55.850
So BJ ran with that story, and that was – he adapted it, and he made it a terrace with flowers.
所以BJ顺着这个故事写下去了，那是——他改编了一下，把它改成了一个长满鲜花的露台。

1362
00:56:57.130 --> 00:57:00.370
But that was a little bit of collaboration there.
但那里有一点合作的成分在里面。

1363
00:57:00.390 --> 00:57:03.270
I think it's such a sweet story, and then it broke my heart.
我觉得这是一个很温馨的故事，然后它却让我心碎。

1364
00:57:03.550 --> 00:57:05.930
Well, Pam then is in the kitchen with Jim.
好吧，接下来帕姆和吉姆在厨房里。

1365
00:57:06.110 --> 00:57:09.290
Her talking head is kind of broken up by this scene in the kitchen.
她的单采镜头被厨房里的这场戏给打断了。

1366
00:57:09.830 --> 00:57:14.890
And she's saying to Jim, Jim is like, wait, you're not going to take the internship?
她对吉姆说，吉姆当时一脸不敢相信，等等，你真的不去实习了吗？

1367
00:57:14.890 --> 00:57:20.450
And she's like, well, you know, like Roy said, there's no guarantee it's going to lead to anything anyway.
而她说，好吧，你知道的，就像罗伊说的，反正这也没有什么前途保证。

1368
00:57:20.690 --> 00:57:21.810
He's like, Roy said that?
吉姆就说，罗伊说过这话？

1369
00:57:22.190 --> 00:57:25.190
And then Pam flips a switch.
然后帕姆瞬间变脸。

1370
00:57:25.370 --> 00:57:26.790
She's like, oh, do you have something to say?
她就说，哦，你有什么高见吗？

1371
00:57:26.930 --> 00:57:29.330
I was like, oh, dang, here we go.
当时我就想，哦，天哪，有好戏看了。

1372
00:57:29.570 --> 00:57:30.250
I know.
我懂。

1373
00:57:30.710 --> 00:57:31.510
She's hurt.
她受伤了。

1374
00:57:31.730 --> 00:57:32.510
She's hurt.
她受伤了。

1375
00:57:33.170 --> 00:57:34.750
And it's not Jim's fault.
而且这并不是吉姆的错。

1376
00:57:34.770 --> 00:57:36.470
He's speaking truth, you know?
他说的是实话，你知道吗？

1377
00:57:36.570 --> 00:57:36.670
I know.
我知道。

1378
00:57:36.830 --> 00:57:37.990
But he's holding that –
但他拿着那个——

1379
00:57:37.990 --> 00:57:39.290
She's like, I'm happy with my choices.
她说，我对自己的选择很满意。

1380
00:57:39.770 --> 00:57:41.410
He's holding that mirror up.
他在她面前举起了一面镜子。

1381
00:57:41.490 --> 00:57:42.790
That's what he does to her.
这就是他对她做的事。

1382
00:57:42.790 --> 00:57:43.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1383
00:57:43.750 --> 00:57:44.010
Ooh.
噢。

1384
00:57:44.290 --> 00:57:45.050
I know.
我知道。

1385
00:57:45.810 --> 00:57:48.210
This is an interesting fan question.
这是一个有趣的粉丝提问。

1386
00:57:48.850 --> 00:57:53.310
Bernardo noted that Jim has a beard when he's talking to Pam in the kitchen.
贝尔纳多注意到吉姆在厨房和帕姆说话时留了胡子。

1387
00:57:53.310 --> 00:57:54.890
And I looked, and he really does.
我仔细一看，还真是。

1388
00:57:55.130 --> 00:57:56.510
He's like very stubbly.
他的胡茬非常明显。

1389
00:57:56.730 --> 00:57:57.170
What?
什么？

1390
00:57:57.450 --> 00:57:59.250
So just to break up that beautiful moment.
所以，就为了破坏那个美妙的时刻。

1391
00:57:59.550 --> 00:58:06.390
Well, Jim says something that really stuck with me, which is he says, you got to take a chance on something sometime.
好吧，吉姆说了一句话让我感触很深，他说，人总得在某些事情上冒险一次。

1392
00:58:06.830 --> 00:58:07.150
Yeah.
对。

1393
00:58:07.450 --> 00:58:10.290
And I thought that was like just a good thing to take away.
我觉得这是一个很棒的感悟。

1394
00:58:11.030 --> 00:58:17.890
Well, we go back to the talking head, and Pam just breaks down.
好了，我们回到单采镜头，帕姆直接崩溃了。

1395
00:58:18.190 --> 00:58:21.450
She's talking about the terrorists, but we know what she's really talking about.
她嘴里说的是露台，但我们都知道她真正指的是什么。

1396
00:58:22.090 --> 00:58:24.130
She says it's just not practical.
她说这根本不切实际。

1397
00:58:24.570 --> 00:58:27.290
You know, you just aren't going to find that.
你知道的，你根本找不到那样的机会。

1398
00:58:27.310 --> 00:58:32.210
And what she's really saying is, I'm never going to have Jim.
而她真正想说的是，我永远也得不到吉姆了。

1399
00:58:32.470 --> 00:58:34.130
I'm never going to have true love.
我永远也得不到真爱了。

1400
00:58:34.450 --> 00:58:36.330
I'm never going to be who I want to be.
我永远也无法成为我想成为的那个人了。

1401
00:58:36.950 --> 00:58:39.330
And that's underneath all of that.
而这一切就压在最底下。

1402
00:58:39.530 --> 00:58:41.730
And also that my dreams aren't valid.
还有我的梦想也是不被认可的。

1403
00:58:42.270 --> 00:58:42.830
Yeah.
对。

1404
00:58:42.910 --> 00:58:44.650
I don't get to even try for my dream.
我甚至连争取一下梦想的机会都没有。

1405
00:58:44.870 --> 00:58:46.130
That's not my path.
那不是我的路。

1406
00:58:46.350 --> 00:58:48.250
A fan question from Adam Falk.
来自亚当·法尔克的粉丝提问。

1407
00:58:48.510 --> 00:58:52.170
He asked, when Roy killed Pam's dream, the tears were so real.
他问，当罗伊扼杀帕姆的梦想时，那眼泪太真实了。

1408
00:58:52.450 --> 00:58:53.570
What were you thinking about?
你当时在想什么？

1409
00:58:54.650 --> 00:58:59.830
Guys, there are times as an actor where your heart just breaks for your character.
各位，作为演员，有时你会由衷地为你的角色感到心碎。

1410
00:59:00.910 --> 00:59:06.510
I just felt her heartbreaking, and it made me cry.
我只是感同身受地觉得她心碎了，这让我哭了出来。

1411
00:59:06.710 --> 00:59:10.490
It's in the same way where it makes you cry when you watch something.
这就跟你看到某些东西时会哭是一样的。

1412
00:59:10.630 --> 00:59:11.930
Or talk about it.
或者谈论它时。

1413
00:59:12.050 --> 00:59:12.310
Yeah.
对。

1414
00:59:12.670 --> 00:59:17.530
I wasn't thinking about, you know, my dead pet or something like that.
我当时并不是在想，你知道的，我死去的宠物或类似的事情。

1415
00:59:17.530 --> 00:59:28.530
I was thinking about how it must feel to have someone not encourage you to feel trapped and to feel so alone.
我在想，当别人不支持你、让你感到被困住且孤立无援时，那种感觉会有多难受。

1416
00:59:28.530 --> 00:59:35.610
And I thought about how the one person who was trying to help me, I just pushed that person away.
我还想到，那个本想帮我的人，却被我给推开了。

1417
00:59:36.510 --> 00:59:38.170
And that kind of makes you cry.
而那种感觉真让人想哭。

1418
00:59:38.610 --> 00:59:44.750
Well, I think our show had a lot of, like, really relatable moments like that.
嗯，我觉得我们的剧里有很多这种很有共鸣的时刻。

1419
00:59:44.890 --> 00:59:46.770
I mean, I know we do these crazy things.
我的意思是，我知道我们做了很多疯狂的事。

1420
00:59:46.770 --> 00:59:52.310
Like, it's going to cut to the warehouse, and Dwight is making a snow angel out of packing peanuts, and there's all of that.
比如，镜头切到仓库，德怀特正用包装用的泡沫塑料块做雪天使，诸如此类的。

1421
00:59:52.310 --> 00:59:58.250
But then I feel like the heart of our show is also just these people living their lives and relationships.
但我觉得我们剧的核心同样也是这些普通人的生活和人际关系。

1422
00:59:58.310 --> 01:00:00.790
And I love that we have that balance.
我很高兴我们能保持这种平衡。

1423
01:00:01.150 --> 01:00:01.550
Me too.
我也是。

1424
01:00:02.150 --> 01:00:07.670
Well, speaking of the warehouse, we cut back down to the warehouse, and Michael has completely destroyed it.
嗯，说到仓库，镜头切回仓库，迈克尔已经把它彻底给毁了。

1425
01:00:08.090 --> 01:00:09.070
He's wrecked it.
他把它搞得一团糟。

1426
01:00:09.110 --> 01:00:09.630
Wrecked it.
一团糟。

1427
01:00:09.710 --> 01:00:11.790
And then he just buys pizza for everyone and leaves.
然后他居然给每个人买了个披萨就走了。

1428
01:00:11.890 --> 01:00:12.470
You know why?
你知道为什么吗？

1429
01:00:12.630 --> 01:00:14.970
Because pizza is the great equalizer.
因为披萨是伟大的平衡器。

1430
01:00:15.710 --> 01:00:16.750
That's what he says.
他是这么说的。

1431
01:00:16.750 --> 01:00:18.410
It's the great equalizer.
这就是伟大的平衡器。

1432
01:00:18.730 --> 01:00:22.170
Well, fan question from Tiffany Ironridge and Pickle Dude.
好，来自蒂凡尼·艾恩里奇和泡菜老弟的粉丝提问。

1433
01:00:22.530 --> 01:00:25.090
How long did it take to clean up the warehouse?
清理仓库花了多长时间？

1434
01:00:25.590 --> 01:00:29.790
And Madeline Albrecht, I feel like this is because she listens to Office Ladies, says,
还有玛德琳·奥尔布雷克，我觉得她是因为听了《办公室女士》节目，所以问：

1435
01:00:29.910 --> 01:00:32.530
was it a hard day for Phil Shea and Michael Gallenberg?
这对菲尔·谢伊和迈克尔·加伦贝格来说是不是个艰难的日子？

1436
01:00:32.890 --> 01:00:34.270
Oh, I love you.
哦，我爱你们。

1437
01:00:34.330 --> 01:00:37.690
And I bet they love you, too, for just even highlighting that.
我敢说他们也会因为你特意提到这点而爱死你的。

1438
01:00:37.930 --> 01:00:40.470
Gina McAdrian said, who cleaned up the mess?
吉娜·麦克阿德里安问，是谁收拾的烂摊子？

1439
01:00:40.630 --> 01:00:41.730
Guys, it was.
伙计们，确实是。

1440
01:00:41.730 --> 01:00:44.450
It was Phil Shea, Michael Gallenberg, their crews.
是菲尔·谢伊、迈克尔·加伦贝格，还有他们的团队。

1441
01:00:44.850 --> 01:00:45.190
Their crew.
他们的团队。

1442
01:00:45.210 --> 01:00:48.530
I don't know how long it took them, but I imagine a long time.
我不知道这花了他们多长时间，但我猜时间不短。

1443
01:00:48.710 --> 01:00:52.290
And also, I think these kind of shoots were more stressful for them because there were
而且我觉得这种拍摄对他们来说压力更大，因为有

1444
01:00:52.290 --> 01:00:56.970
big prop moments that the whole scene was centered around.
整个场景都围绕着的重要道具时刻。

1445
01:00:57.230 --> 01:00:57.350
Yeah.
对。

1446
01:00:57.350 --> 01:00:59.230
And they had to have everything ready.
而且他们必须把一切都准备就绪。

1447
01:00:59.630 --> 01:01:03.390
When Michael opened up the bag of packing peanuts, they had to have a backup one.
当迈克尔打开那袋泡沫塑料时，他们必须备好一个替补的。

1448
01:01:03.510 --> 01:01:03.670
Yep.
没错。

1449
01:01:03.890 --> 01:01:05.470
They had to have all of that ready to go.
他们必须把所有这些都准备妥当。

1450
01:01:05.630 --> 01:01:07.690
If you get a chance, watch the deleted scenes.
如果你有机会，去看一下被删减的片段。

1451
01:01:07.690 --> 01:01:11.070
There is one that I loved so much in this.
这里面有一个我非常喜欢。

1452
01:01:11.170 --> 01:01:14.670
It has nothing to do with this episode, really, the story at all.
其实这跟这一集的内容完全没关系，跟剧情也毫无关系。

1453
01:01:15.510 --> 01:01:17.770
Michael is trying to set his ringtone.
迈克尔在试图设置他的手机铃声。

1454
01:01:18.150 --> 01:01:21.470
Oh, and he's asking Pam to help him pick a ringtone.
哦，而且他让帕姆帮他挑铃声。

1455
01:01:21.670 --> 01:01:22.750
Yes, and Jim is there, too.
对，吉姆也在那儿。

1456
01:01:22.910 --> 01:01:27.070
And it's just these little small ridiculous moments that crack me up.
这些细小而荒谬的瞬间总是能把我逗乐。

1457
01:01:27.190 --> 01:01:29.410
We had a lot of those that we would shoot.
我们拍过很多这样的镜头。

1458
01:01:29.550 --> 01:01:31.670
They were just office life moments.
它们就是办公室生活的瞬间。

1459
01:01:31.810 --> 01:01:31.990
Yeah.
对。

1460
01:01:32.130 --> 01:01:35.410
And so often, those were the things that would have to get cut for time.
而且通常，这些镜头往往会因为时间不够而被剪掉。

1461
01:01:35.410 --> 01:01:36.050
I know.
我知道。

1462
01:01:36.310 --> 01:01:40.130
But they're now a treasure living on the DVD extras.
但现在它们成了活在DVD花絮里的宝藏。

1463
01:01:41.250 --> 01:01:50.350
At 19 minutes, 52 seconds, I want you to notice, we imply that everyone from the warehouse is walking back upstairs.
在19分52秒的时候，我想请大家注意，我们暗示仓库里的所有人都正走回楼上。

1464
01:01:50.350 --> 01:01:55.590
I want you to notice that just Michael, Kevin, and Dwight go into the door at the top of the stairs.
我想让你们注意，只有迈克尔、凯文和德怀特走进了楼梯顶部的门。

1465
01:01:56.250 --> 01:02:00.190
That's, again, because it's just a closet, and that was as many people as they could fit.
那又是因为那其实只是个储藏室，那是他们能挤进去的最多人数了。

1466
01:02:00.290 --> 01:02:01.370
Right, and that was tight.
没错，而且空间很挤。

1467
01:02:01.370 --> 01:02:06.350
And then in the next shot, you see them walking into the office.
然后在下一个镜头里，你看到他们走进了办公室。

1468
01:02:06.490 --> 01:02:07.670
Michael's carrying a pizza.
迈克尔手里拿着一个披萨。

1469
01:02:08.310 --> 01:02:11.170
But we shot that on a completely different day.
但我们是在完全不同的一天拍的那个镜头。

1470
01:02:11.450 --> 01:02:11.650
Yeah.
对。

1471
01:02:11.890 --> 01:02:24.230
So Veda, our script supervisor, she would have written down which hand Michael was carrying the pizza box in so that she could hand him that pizza box then on the next day and say,
所以我们的场记维达，她会记下迈克尔是用哪只手拿着披萨盒的，这样她就能在第二天把那个披萨盒递给他，然后说，

1472
01:02:24.350 --> 01:02:25.250
all right, here it is.
好了，给你。

1473
01:02:25.250 --> 01:02:30.490
Although sometimes they would have conversations that were like, well, I could believe that you switched hands on the way up.
虽然有时候他们会讨论说，嗯，我倒觉得你可能在走上楼的途中换了手。

1474
01:02:30.490 --> 01:02:31.570
We would have deep conversations.
我们会进行深入的讨论。

1475
01:02:31.910 --> 01:02:32.430
We would have deep conversations.
我们会进行深入的讨论。

1476
01:02:32.690 --> 01:02:36.230
Do you think he switched the pizza box from one hand to the other while he was walking?
你觉得他在走路的时候把披萨盒从一只手换到了另一只手吗？

1477
01:02:36.410 --> 01:02:38.350
Because maybe he had to use that hand to open the door.
因为也许他得用那只手去开门。

1478
01:02:38.530 --> 01:02:39.490
Yes, exactly.
对，没错。

1479
01:02:39.670 --> 01:02:40.290
Yeah, exactly.
对，没错。

1480
01:02:40.310 --> 01:02:41.670
So perhaps, you know what, it's fine.
所以也许，你知道吗，没关系。

1481
01:02:41.690 --> 01:02:42.950
You can carry it in either hand.
你用哪只手拿都行。

1482
01:02:42.950 --> 01:02:51.190
Well, I was really bummed that at the Women in the Workplace, there was no food because I was really excited that we might have pizza too.
嗯，我真的很沮丧，在“职场女性”会议上没有提供食物，因为我本来真的很兴奋，以为我们可能也会有披萨吃呢。

1483
01:02:52.470 --> 01:02:53.710
I mean, you know.
我是说，你懂的。

1484
01:02:53.930 --> 01:02:55.590
This was Jan's big fail.
这是简的重大失误。

1485
01:02:55.750 --> 01:02:57.130
If she would have just fed us.
如果她当时能管管我们的饭就好了。

1486
01:02:57.430 --> 01:02:58.370
Snacks or something.
零食什么的。

1487
01:02:58.710 --> 01:03:02.230
But, you know, Mindy and I, Ed Helms, we love prop food.
但是，你知道，明迪和我，还有艾德·海姆斯，我们都很喜欢道具食物。

1488
01:03:03.750 --> 01:03:08.330
Well, this episode ends with Pam answering the phone.
嗯，这一集的结尾是帕姆接电话。

1489
01:03:08.570 --> 01:03:10.250
Dunder Mifflin, this is Pam.
邓德米夫林，我是帕姆。

1490
01:03:10.470 --> 01:03:16.910
And this is really significant because in her fight with Jim, he says to her, what, do you really want to be a receptionist your whole life?
这非常重要，因为在她和吉姆的争吵中，吉姆对她说，怎么，你真的想当一辈子前台吗？

1491
01:03:17.370 --> 01:03:20.730
And so we end with her being a receptioniSt.
所以我们以她作为前台结束了这一集。

1492
01:03:20.870 --> 01:03:22.890
And she just looks at him.
而她只是看着他。

1493
01:03:23.050 --> 01:03:23.370
Yeah.
对。

1494
01:03:23.610 --> 01:03:24.370
There's this moment.
有这样一个瞬间。

1495
01:03:24.610 --> 01:03:25.790
It's unresolved.
这事还没解决。

1496
01:03:25.990 --> 01:03:27.250
Their fight is unresolved.
他们的争吵还没有结果。

1497
01:03:27.510 --> 01:03:28.310
And that's it.
就是这样。

1498
01:03:28.390 --> 01:03:29.290
That's boys and girls.
这就是《男女之间》。

1499
01:03:32.230 --> 01:03:32.910
C.G.
C.G.

1500
01:03:33.370 --> 01:03:43.990
wrote in to say, I would really love for you guys to keep track, because we've been tracking things, of when Jim changes from classic fit to slim fit shirts.
来信说，我真的很想让你们记录一下，因为我们一直在统计，吉姆是什么时候从经典修身衬衫换成修身衬衫的。

1501
01:03:44.470 --> 01:03:46.270
Oh, he has such a baggy shirt.
哦，他的衬衫太宽松了。

1502
01:03:46.270 --> 01:03:47.870
I noticed that in this episode.
我在这一集里也注意到了。

1503
01:03:47.990 --> 01:03:48.170
Yeah.
是啊。

1504
01:03:48.370 --> 01:03:49.670
There's a shot of him.
有一个他的镜头。

1505
01:03:49.790 --> 01:03:52.590
He's kind of reclined back eating his pizza and his shirt's untucked.
他有点靠在后面吃披萨，衬衫也没扎进裤子里。

1506
01:03:52.670 --> 01:03:58.170
And I'm like, that shirt, it looks like it's the 90s where everyone's clothes was like three sizes too big for them.
当时我就想，那件衬衫看起来就像90年代一样，当时所有人的衣服都比他们大个三号。

1507
01:03:58.170 --> 01:04:07.490
Yeah, you're going to notice eventually, and we'll talk about this, Pam stops wearing her hair in a clip, Jim stops having a shaggy hairdo,
对，你迟早会发现的，我们也会聊到这个，潘不再用夹子夹头发了，吉姆也不留蓬乱的发型了，

1508
01:04:07.630 --> 01:04:10.410
and he starts getting some better fitting suits.
而且他开始穿更合身的西装。

1509
01:04:10.630 --> 01:04:11.250
I agree.
我同意。

1510
01:04:11.330 --> 01:04:12.530
So we'll be clocking all of that.
所以我们会记录所有这些变化。

1511
01:04:12.590 --> 01:04:14.250
You guys, we're going to track it all.
伙计们，我们会全程追踪的。

1512
